solutions.body:
The angles add up to $360^\circ$. Four acute angles would add up to less than $360^\circ$, so 4 is impossible. All of 0–3 occur:
- 0: a rectangle;
- 1: a right trapezoid with angles $90^\circ, 90^\circ, 60^\circ, 120^\circ$;
- 2: a parallelogram with angles $60^\circ, 120^\circ, 60^\circ, 120^\circ$;
- 3: angles $80^\circ, 80^\circ, 80^\circ, 120^\circ$ (any four angles below $180^\circ$ adding to $360^\circ$ can be realised by a convex quadrilateral).

**Answer: (B) 0, 1, 2, 3**
